                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse2"><span><strong>Q2:</strong> Do you create custom-designed websites for authors or use templates?</span></div></div><div id="collapse2" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Custom-designed. Every author website we build starts with original design work based on your genre, your books, your audience, and your brand identity. We don't purchase a template and drop your content into it. Your site's visual identity, layout, typography, colour palette, imagery style, page structure, is designed specifically for you and your readership. The result is a website that feels like it belongs to your author brand rather than one that looks interchangeable with hundreds of other authors using the same purchased theme.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse3"><span><strong>Q3:</strong> Can the website include book listings, reviews, and purchase links?</span></div></div><div id="collapse3" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, and it should. We build dedicated book pages for each title featuring cover images, descriptions, review quotes, series information, and direct purchase links to Amazon, Apple Books, Kobo, Barnes & Noble, and any other retailer or direct sales platform you use. For authors with multiple titles, we create catalogue pages that let visitors browse your complete body of work filtered by series, genre, or format. The goal is making the path from "this looks interesting" to "I just bought it" as short and seamless as possible.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse4"><span><strong>Q4:</strong> How long does it take to build an author website?</span></div></div><div id="collapse4" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>A standard author website typically takes three to five weeks from initial consultation to launch, accounting for design, feedback rounds, development, content setup, and SEO implementation. Larger or more complex sites with extensive book catalogues, custom functionality, ecommerce integration, or significant content migration from an existing site take longer. We'll give you a clear timeline during your consultation based on your specific project scope, and we communicate throughout if anything shifts.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse5"><span><strong>Q5:</strong> Do you provide mobile-friendly and responsive website designs?</span></div></div><div id="collapse5" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, every site we build is fully responsive, designed to display and function correctly across desktop computers, laptops, tablets, and mobile phones. Given that the majority of web traffic now comes from mobile devices, responsive design isn't an optional feature. It's foundational. Your site will look professional and navigate smoothly regardless of what device a reader is using to visit it.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse6"><span><strong>Q6:</strong> Can I update my website content myself after it is built?</span></div></div><div id="collapse6" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. We build on WordPress specifically because it allows non-technical users to update content independently, adding new book listings, publishing blog posts, updating event information, changing images, and making routine content updates without needing a developer. You receive a training session and written documentation covering every task you're likely to need. For anything beyond routine content updates, structural changes, new feature additions, design modifications, we offer ongoing support packages or one-off development work as needed.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse7"><span><strong>Q7:</strong> Do you include SEO services to help readers find my website?</span></div></div><div id="collapse7" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, foundational SEO is built into every website we develop. This includes optimised page titles and meta descriptions, proper heading structure, image optimisation, schema markup for books and authors, XML sitemap generation, site speed optimisation, and mobile usability, the technical infrastructure that search engines need to properly index and rank your site. For authors who want more aggressive search visibility, ongoing content strategy, keyword targeting for genre-specific terms, backlink development, we offer additional SEO services beyond the standard build.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse8"><span><strong>Q8:</strong> How much does author website development cost in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse8" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>The cost of website development in Melbourne for authors depends on the scope of the project, how many pages, how much custom design work, which features and integrations are included, and whether additional services like content writing or advanced SEO are part of the build. A focused launch site with a handful of pages costs less than a comprehensive author platform with a full book catalogue, blog, email integration, media kit, and ecommerce functionality. We quote individually based on your specific requirements, get in touch and we'll give you transparent pricing with a clear breakdown of what's included.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse9"><span><strong>Q9:</strong> Can you integrate blogs and newsletters into the website?</span></div></div><div id="collapse9" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, both are standard features in our author website builds. Your blog is built on WordPress with full publishing functionality, categories, tags, featured images, scheduling, and SEO optimisation for every post. Newsletter integration connects your site to your preferred email platform, Mailchimp, ConvertKit, MailerLite, or others, with signup forms, landing pages, and automated welcome sequences positioned strategically throughout your site to convert visitors into subscribers. Both features are essential for authors building long-term readership between book releases.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse10"><span><strong>Q10:</strong> Do you offer ongoing maintenance and support after launch?</span></div></div><div id="collapse10" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes. We offer ongoing maintenance packages covering WordPress updates, plugin updates, security monitoring, regular backups, uptime monitoring, and technical support for any issues that arise after launch. We also provide on-demand development support for authors who need occasional changes, new features, or design updates without committing to a monthly retainer. Your website is a long-term asset, keeping it secure, updated, and functioning properly after launch matters as much as building it right in the first place.</p></div></div></div>
